{"name":"Sky City","hex":"#a0bdd9","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"}],"entries":[{"title":"DJI Sky City","blocks":[{"text":"DJI Sky City is a two-tower office complex in Nanshan, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China. It is owned by DJI and serves as its global corporate headquarters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJI_Sky_City"},{"title":"Sky City (Changsha)","blocks":[{"text":"Sky City, or Sky City One, was an 838-metre-tall (2,749 ft) planned skyscraper in the city of Changsha, Hunan in south-central China. The prospective builders, Broad Sustainable Building, estimated it would take just 90 days to construct. Including the 120 days needed for prefabrication before on-site work commenced, the total time needed was 210 days. Pre-construction activities were halted in August 2013 after government regulators required additional approvals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/J220_Sky_City_Changsha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_City_(Changsha)"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-DJI_Headquarters_Tower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADJI_Headquarters_Tower_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/J220_Sky_City_Changsha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/J220_Sky_City_Changsha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJ220_Sky_City_Changsha.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/500px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.j